{"text": "DEFENSE INFORMATION SYSTEMS AGENCY\n\nP.O. BOX 549\nFORT MEADE, MARYLAND 20755-0549\n\nnferto General Counsel January 7, 2014\nFOIA Office\n\nMuckRock News\nATTN: Jason Smathers\nDEPT MR 8404\nP.O. Box 55819\nBoston, MA 02205-5819\n\nRE: FOIA 14-02\nDear Mr. Smathers:\n\nThis letter is a response to your Freedom of Information request for a copy of the FOIA log for\nthe Defense Information Systems Agency for FY2013.\n\nThere were thirteen pages responsive to your request. All information pertaining to privacy\nrequests have been redacted pursuant to 5 U.S.C. \u00a7552 b(6). Those numbers are: 13-01, 13-02,\n13-05, 13-06, 13-09, 13-14, 13-15, 13-25, 13-26, 13-30, 13-31, 13-32, 13-34, 13-35, 13-36,\n13-41, 13-45, 13-47, 13-48, and 13-50.\n\nDue to the national emergency declared by the President in the aftermath of the terrorist attacks\nof September 11, 2001, the Department of Defense (DoD) has reviewed its policy regarding the\nrelease of names and identifying information of personnel not assigned to units protected from\nrelease by statute (10 USC \u00a7 130b). As a result of this review, it has been determined that\nrelease of lists of names of personnel would constitute a clearly unwarranted invasion of the\npersonal privacy of those individuals. Accordingly, the information you requested is exempt\nfrom release pursuant to 5 USC \u00a7 552 b(6).\n\nExemption 6 - Applies to information, which if released, could reasonably be expected to\nconstitute a clearly unwarranted invasion of personal privacy of an individual.\n\nYou may appeal this partial denial by writing to the Director, Defense Information Systems\nAgency, P.O. Box 549, Ft. Meade, MD 20755, within 60 days of your receipt this letter. Both\nthe letter and envelope should be clearly marked \"Freedom of Information Act Appeal.\"",
